  "title": "1887 Yellow River Flood",
  "summary": "In 1887 heavy rain pushed the Yellow River over its dikes in Henan Province, with breaches reported near Zhengzhou. The flood covered about 50,000 square miles, swamped eleven large towns and hundreds of villages, and left two million homeless. Death tolls quoted run from about 900,000 to two million.",
